The reality is when you're in the IELTS&nbsp;test, you're not trying to use vocabulary that&nbsp;nobody knows.

00:06:59.579 --> 00:07:02.934
You're trying to use vocabulary that&nbsp;everybody knows.&nbsp;

00:07:02.934 --> 00:07:07.787
Using normal everyday vocabulary&nbsp;is what will get you a high score.

00:07:07.787 --> 00:07:11.887
But it's using&nbsp;it accurately and using it in the correct context.

00:07:12.196 --> 00:07:22.175
&nbsp;And then, for whatever topic that you're discussing,&nbsp;having that specific topic-related language that&nbsp;will show that you have a wide range is what gets&nbsp;you a high score.&nbsp;

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:29.706
So if you've been learning&nbsp;special words for the IELTS test that you think are impressive and that will get you a high&nbsp;score,

00:07:29.706 --> 00:07:35.975
what you see from Julia's performance here&nbsp;is that, that is not what the examiner is actually&nbsp;looking for.

00:07:36.491 --> 00:07:40.734
